"NameComponent gives entities app-level names, but it leaks meaning the ecs entity! macro layer cannot have (e.g. resolving blob references by name), forces uniqueness hacks (map-gen rooms must stay nameless), and conflates display naming with identity lookup. Eliminate it: every kind of asset gets its own named asset table (name unique within that kind's namespace), and long-lived referenceable entities (e.g. allegiances) are instantiated FROM named assets with a recorded asset->entity mapping (like special_entity_blobs today). Entity-reference resolution then looks up asset name -> instantiated entity id, never a component name. Display naming becomes a separate concern (appearance/narration), not an identity component. Related: validate-unique-asset-names-within-each-namespace (the uniqueness rule per kind) and name-canonical-incremental-asset-updates-no-full-replacement (names as canonical asset identity). Sequencing: entity-blob stable refs does NOT block on this -- its resolver is injected at the app layer, which may interim-resolve via from_name and switch to asset-name lookup when this lands."